## 11. UI Implementation with Shadcn-ui & Tailwind CSS

UI elements MUST be implemented by installing Shadcn/ui components and styling them with Tailwind CSS utility classes. Prioritize matching the UI/UX descriptions in the user stories.

### Mandatory Test ID Requirements
**ALL interactive elements MUST include data-testid attributes for E2E testing reliability:**

#### Form Elements
- **Inputs**: `data-testid="input-{fieldname}"` (e.g., `data-testid="input-email"`)
- **Buttons**: `data-testid="button-{action}"` (e.g., `data-testid="button-submit"`, `data-testid="button-login"`)
- **Checkboxes/Radio**: `data-testid="checkbox-{name}"` (e.g., `data-testid="checkbox-terms"`)
- **Select/Dropdown**: `data-testid="select-{name}"` (e.g., `data-testid="select-country"`)

#### Navigation Elements
- **Links**: `data-testid="link-{destination}"` (e.g., `data-testid="link-login"`, `data-testid="link-register"`)
- **Menu Items**: `data-testid="nav-{section}"` (e.g., `data-testid="nav-features"`)

#### Content Areas
- **Sections**: `data-testid="section-{name}"` (e.g., `data-testid="section-hero"`, `data-testid="section-pricing"`)
- **Cards**: `data-testid="card-{type}"` (e.g., `data-testid="card-pricing-sprout"`)
- **Modals**: `data-testid="modal-{purpose}"` (e.g., `data-testid="modal-confirmation"`)

#### Error/Success States
- **Error Messages**: `data-testid="error-{field}"` (e.g., `data-testid="error-email"`)
- **Success Messages**: `data-testid="success-{action}"` (e.g., `data-testid="success-registration"`)
- **Loading States**: `data-testid="loading-{action}"` (e.g., `data-testid="loading-submit"`)

#### Example Implementation
```tsx
// ❌ BAD - No test ID
<Button onClick={handleSubmit}>Register</Button>

// ✅ GOOD - With test ID
<Button data-testid="button-register" onClick={handleSubmit}>Register</Button>

// ❌ BAD - No test ID  
<input type="email" placeholder="Email" />

// ✅ GOOD - With test ID
<input data-testid="input-email" type="email" placeholder="Email" />
```

### Benefits
- **Reliable E2E tests** - Independent of UI text changes
- **Faster test execution** - Direct element targeting
- **Better debugging** - Clear element identification

- **Maintainable tests** - Stable locators that don't break with design changes